d technology, but not willing to further education. Also note that C is egocentric and difficulty communicating ideas. We can argue that while reliability is high, the egocentric attitude could impair crew cooperation, which is critical. Maybe we suggest Candidate B as alternative because of stress resilience and conscientiousness, but B makes nasty remarks, which is also a problem. Or D takes responsibility seriously, solves problems well, but has hot temper and know-it-all attitude.\n\nWe need to make a focused argumentative contribution: state current recommendation (maybe still C, but note concerns). Or we could shift recommendation to B if we think stress resilience outweighs communication issues. But we need to reference Agent 1's point. Let's say we agree with C but highlight the need to verify communication and egocentric behavior. Provide evidence: C keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology, but not willing to further education. So we can say we still recommend C but we need to probe further.\n\nThus our vote remains Candidate C. Provide reasoning.\n\nProceed."}
